                <pb facs="0461" n="449" xml:id="pg449"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.199/51: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Seville</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bay</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Seville</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-11-13T13:00:00+00:00">November 13, 1937—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 4:07 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s November 11, 5 p.m. General Queipo de Llano stated today that
                    General Franco had authorized the return of Consul Chapman to Bilbao and that he
                    would telegraph at once with a view to facilitating his entry at Irun.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bay</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
